WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.606 --> 00:00:10.372
34. 35. Okay. that's everybody.
Okay. First stop is the touch pool.

2
00:00:10.443 --> 00:00:13.241
Line up at the dolphin gate.
Oh. stay with your buddy.

3
00:00:13.313 --> 00:00:15.611
Make sure you watch your step
as you enter the aquarium.

4
00:00:19.552 --> 00:00:22.988
We did it. Gus. A year of
planning's finally paid off.

5
00:00:23.423 --> 00:00:26.051
Don't you think we should wait
until they get a little further away?

6
00:00:26.126 --> 00:00:27.650
No. We have to move now.

7
00:00:28.061 --> 00:00:31.497
We've got 10 minutes to find a
dolphin. feed it. then ride it.

8
00:00:31.798 --> 00:00:32.822
Plus. my dad being sick

9
00:00:32.899 --> 00:00:35.595
and not being able to
chaperone. the fates are with us.

10
00:00:35.668 --> 00:00:37.033
It's a perfect storm.

11
00:00:37.103 --> 00:00:38.536
I don't want to
miss the otters.

12
00:00:38.605 --> 00:00:42.268
No. we won't. Um... You brought
your dad's camera. right?

13
00:00:44.811 --> 00:00:46.244
You're not sick.

14
00:00:46.413 --> 00:00:48.005
And you're not
very thorough.

15
00:00:49.049 --> 00:00:50.073
How did you know?

16
00:00:50.150 --> 00:00:53.142
Oh. maybe it's that snorkel
hanging out of your backpack.

17
00:00:53.219 --> 00:00:56.086
What kind of undercover operation
are you running here. kid?

18
00:00:56.156 --> 00:00:58.989
Plus. you left
this behind.

19
00:01:04.397 --> 00:01:07.628
If you're going to take time to
create a deception. do it better.

20
00:01:08.568 --> 00:01:11.594
Wait. Dad. I'm confused.
You want me to lie to you?

21
00:01:12.038 --> 00:01:13.403
No.

22
00:01:14.474 --> 00:01:17.637
I want you to make it more of
a challenge for me to catch you.

23
00:01:19.946 --> 00:01:21.846
Because
I always will.

24
00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:29.074
Advertise your product or brand here
contact www.OpenSubtitles.org today

25
00:01:30.757 --> 00:01:32.748
Wait a minute.
Something's wrong.

26
00:01:32.826 --> 00:01:36.057
What do you mean? I mean
this doesn't add up. Gus.

27
00:01:37.630 --> 00:01:38.995
There's not really
a burglary ring

28
00:01:39.099 --> 00:01:40.623
at a gentlemen's
finishing school. is there?

29
00:01:40.700 --> 00:01:43.032
I'm sorry. Shawn. I made
up the thing about the case.

30
00:01:43.103 --> 00:01:44.764
I needed you to come down
here to do me a favor.

31
00:01:44.838 --> 00:01:46.032
Well. you know what?
This is a bad time.

32
00:01:46.106 --> 00:01:47.539
My dad just got
a new fishing boat

33
00:01:47.607 --> 00:01:49.541
and insists on taking me
out to kill innocent fish.

34
00:01:49.609 --> 00:01:52.077
And I can only avoid
so many things at the same

35
00:01:52.378 --> 00:01:53.367
time.

36
00:01:54.080 --> 00:01:55.547
All right.
What is it?

37
00:01:56.282 --> 00:01:57.613
It's a funeral.

38
00:01:57.684 --> 00:02:01.518
No. Absolutely not. You know I
hate funerals. They're depressing.

39
00:02:01.588 --> 00:02:05.547
There's organ music. and six times out
of ten. there's a snake in the casket.

40
00:02:05.859 --> 00:02:09.420
We'll just go really quick.
I need someone to support me.

41
00:02:12.799 --> 00:02:14.528
All right. Who's it for?

42
00:02:22.542 --> 00:02:24.669
Would you please
just tell me who died?

43
00:02:24.744 --> 00:02:26.541
I don't like all this
secrecy. Gus.

44
00:02:26.613 --> 00:02:28.103
And what's with
the aquatic theme.

45
00:02:28.181 --> 00:02:30.149
all this Ocean
Society stuff?

46
00:02:30.216 --> 00:02:31.615
Did Jack Costo die?

47
00:02:31.684 --> 00:02:34.118
Jacques Cousteau
died in 1995.

48
00:02:34.187 --> 00:02:35.518
Well. I don't think
these people got the memo.

49
00:02:35.989 --> 00:02:38.082
Come on. who died?
Who was it?

50
00:02:38.158 --> 00:02:39.716
One of those guys?
The boat guys?

51
00:02:39.792 --> 00:02:41.692
Huh? Was there
some kind of accident?

52
00:02:43.630 --> 00:02:44.722
Dude. I got it.

53
00:02:45.198 --> 00:02:46.859
It's the guy with the
horn-rimmed glasses.

54
00:02:47.200 --> 00:02:50.931
If there was ever somebody
with one foot in the grave...

55
00:02:52.672 --> 00:02:53.730
Sorry.

56
00:02:54.707 --> 00:02:56.299
You know. the camera
adds 10 years.

57
00:02:56.376 --> 00:02:58.139
It's 10 pounds.
Shh. Just shh.

58
00:03:06.953 --> 00:03:08.045
Wait a minute.

59
00:03:10.223 --> 00:03:12.123
Is this a funeral
for a sea lion?

60
00:03:12.825 --> 00:03:16.056
Yes. Yes. it is.
And don't start. Shawn.

61
00:03:16.129 --> 00:03:17.994
Shabby's more
than just a sea lion.

62
00:03:18.064 --> 00:03:20.032
He's a local hero
and a heartwarming story.

63
00:03:20.099 --> 00:03:22.727
I can't believe you made me put on a
dress shirt for something with flippers.

64
00:03:22.802 --> 00:03:26.363
The ocean is a little
smaller today

65
00:03:26.439 --> 00:03:30.432
with the loss of this
inspirational guy.

66
00:03:31.277 --> 00:03:33.541
Is that Randy LaBayda? Dude!

67
00:03:34.180 --> 00:03:35.909
They got Randy LaBayda
from Animal Planet.

68
00:03:35.982 --> 00:03:40.078
Shh! If sea creatures could
cry. their tears would cause

69
00:03:40.153 --> 00:03:43.748
the water level of all
the oceans of the world

70
00:03:44.023 --> 00:03:47.186
to rise an alarming
two-and-a-half inches.

71
00:03:47.760 --> 00:03:50.422
But Shabby would
want us to rejoice.

72
00:03:50.496 --> 00:03:53.226
I was the last person
to see him alive

73
00:03:53.299 --> 00:03:55.824
and some people think
I'm crazy to believe this.

74
00:03:56.169 --> 00:04:00.629
but as I returned him to
his home. Sweet Mother Ocean.

75
00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:05.504
I thought I actually
saw him wink at me.

76
00:04:05.778 --> 00:04:08.144
Just how famous
was this sea lion?

77
00:04:08.214 --> 00:04:10.580
He's the big
local story of the year.

78
00:04:10.650 --> 00:04:13.517
He was rescued by the aquarium
people. Shawn. Remember?

79
00:04:13.586 --> 00:04:15.713
Floating on that
loose raft.

80
00:04:15.788 --> 00:04:18.382
Then he died tragically after
being released out into the wild.

81
00:04:18.791 --> 00:04:20.383
Come and grieve.

82
00:04:20.727 --> 00:04:24.185
It's a poignant story. and I need
you to support me in my time of need.

83
00:04:25.865 --> 00:04:28.663
You've got to be kidding me.
This is an open casket?

84
00:04:31.004 --> 00:04:32.301
Shabby.

85
00:04:33.873 --> 00:04:35.807
You almost made it.

86
00:04:37.443 --> 00:04:40.810
But you touched our hearts
and our souls.

87
00:04:41.648 --> 00:04:44.242
Be free swimming
in the ocean of heaven.

88
00:04:44.317 --> 00:04:46.046
where there are
no natural predators.

89
00:04:46.586 --> 00:04:47.985
Good speech.

90
00:04:48.154 --> 00:04:49.519
Your turn.

91
00:04:50.823 --> 00:04:51.949
You kidding me?

92
00:04:55.862 --> 00:04:57.523
Shabby. buddy.

93
00:04:58.531 --> 00:05:00.761
You lived a full life.
I guess.

94
00:05:01.401 --> 00:05:03.699
Uh. probably balanced
a beach ball on your nose

95
00:05:03.770 --> 00:05:05.362
At some point.

96
00:05:06.339 --> 00:05:08.534
Maybe honked a horn
with your mouth

97
00:05:09.542 --> 00:05:12.602
<i>or barked the melody
of Grand Old Flag.</i>

98
00:05:13.112 --> 00:05:16.343
Clearly.
you ate very well.

99
00:05:21.354 --> 00:05:22.582
Oh. no.

100
00:05:23.556 --> 00:05:25.387
"Oh. no" what?

101
00:05:25.458 --> 00:05:27.449
I think this sea lion
was murdered.

102
00:05:31.798 --> 00:05:35.290
<i>I know. you know
That I'm not telling the truth</i>

103
00:05:35.368 --> 00:05:38.531
<i>I know. you know
They just don't have any proof</i>

104
00:05:38.604 --> 00:05:41.630
<i>Embrace the deception
Learn how to bend</i>

105
00:05:41.708 --> 00:05:46.042
<i>Your worst inhibitions tend
to psych you out in the end</i>

106
00:05:51.384 --> 00:05:53.944
Why do you hate me?
I don't hate you.

107
00:05:54.020 --> 00:05:56.420
I'm telling you. there's
something unnatural going on here.

108
00:05:56.489 --> 00:05:59.049
We should go back to the aquarium to
check out Shabby's cage or something.

109
00:05:59.125 --> 00:06:01.457
He wasn't in an exhibit.
He was in the ocean.

110
00:06:01.527 --> 00:06:03.392
He was released back into
the wild three days ago.

111
00:06:03.463 --> 00:06:06.660
Gentlemen. I'm gonna need
to see you for a moment.

112
00:06:07.266 --> 00:06:09.257
Great. now you got me
kicked out of a funeral.

113
00:06:09.435 --> 00:06:11.062
Nice. Just add it
to the list.

114
00:06:11.137 --> 00:06:13.469
Kicked out of PetSmart.
Kicked out of Santa's Village.

115
00:06:13.539 --> 00:06:14.597
Kicked out of
the Salvation Army.

116
00:06:14.674 --> 00:06:16.232
Dishonorably discharged.

117
00:06:17.176 --> 00:06:19.474
Now. what do you mean...
I apologize.

118
00:06:19.545 --> 00:06:21.638
He's angry because I
tricked him into coming.

119
00:06:21.714 --> 00:06:22.976
I am a conservationist.

120
00:06:23.049 --> 00:06:25.313
I am an annual pass holder
at the aquarium.

121
00:06:25.385 --> 00:06:28.286
I am a registered aqua-blogger
with topic-starting privileges

122
00:06:28.354 --> 00:06:30.549
and level three-thread management
on the sea lion message boards...

123
00:06:30.623 --> 00:06:35.185
No. I want to know what you
mean. "He was murdered. "

124
00:06:36.729 --> 00:06:38.993
I'm a psychic. I work
with the SBPD.

125
00:06:39.065 --> 00:06:40.726
I also make
my own saltwater taffy.

126
00:06:40.800 --> 00:06:42.165
Wait a minute.
What...

127
00:06:42.402 --> 00:06:43.835
Why do you ask that?

128
00:06:44.270 --> 00:06:47.865
Because I've seen some suspicious
things at that aquarium.

129
00:06:50.743 --> 00:06:51.971
We can't talk here.

130
00:06:52.345 --> 00:06:53.437
Is there somewhere
we can meet?

131
00:06:53.513 --> 00:06:54.502
Yes.

132
00:06:59.185 --> 00:07:00.243
Dude. what are you doing?

133
00:07:00.319 --> 00:07:01.343
Cleaning up.

134
00:07:01.421 --> 00:07:03.355
But why?
This place is a mess.

135
00:07:03.423 --> 00:07:05.618
And it's not all the time that we
have an attractive conservationist

136
00:07:05.691 --> 00:07:07.056
come by the office.

137
00:07:07.126 --> 00:07:09.720
Oh. and by the way.
I call her.

138
00:07:09.796 --> 00:07:12.390
What do you mean. you call
her? You can't call a person.

139
00:07:12.465 --> 00:07:13.489
Why not?

140
00:07:13.566 --> 00:07:14.999
'Cause I already called her
at the funeral.

141
00:07:15.067 --> 00:07:17.126
You did not.
She touched me. Gus.

142
00:07:17.203 --> 00:07:18.465
That's because you
bumped into her.

143
00:07:19.772 --> 00:07:23.674
It doesn't matter. Contact is
contact. It's the rule. buddy.

144
00:07:23.743 --> 00:07:27.110
You know what?
Get ready for battle.

145
00:07:27.180 --> 00:07:29.148
"Get ready for battle"?
Come on.

146
00:07:29.215 --> 00:07:30.273
Yep.

147
00:07:30.349 --> 00:07:32.943
This is ridiculous. We can't go to
battle over a girl we don't know.

148
00:07:33.019 --> 00:07:34.418
I'll back off.

149
00:07:34.487 --> 00:07:36.751
You'll back off? Why?

150
00:07:36.956 --> 00:07:40.050
Because this is silly. Look.
you do your thing. you work it.

151
00:07:40.126 --> 00:07:41.753
and I'll stay
out of the way.

152
00:07:41.828 --> 00:07:43.625
You think I can't get
a girl on my own!

153
00:07:43.796 --> 00:07:45.491
Fine. I'll back off.

154
00:07:45.565 --> 00:07:47.396
I already backed off!
Too bad!

155
00:07:47.467 --> 00:07:49.196
Backed off what?

156
00:07:52.038 --> 00:07:54.666
Well. I was in charge
of Shabby's rehabilitation.

157
00:07:54.740 --> 00:07:58.198
And a lot of unexplained
things happened.

158
00:07:58.277 --> 00:08:02.714
First of all. they moved up the
date of his release by six days.

159
00:08:02.915 --> 00:08:05.179
And why did
they do that?

160
00:08:06.018 --> 00:08:09.681
Well. um. Randy LaBayda.

161
00:08:10.089 --> 00:08:13.422
Randy LaBayda?
From the funeral?

162
00:08:13.626 --> 00:08:16.959
<i>And Pacific Ocean
Aqua Patrol. Yeah.</i>

163
00:08:17.430 --> 00:08:19.694
I used to watch that show after
wrestling practice in high school.

164
00:08:19.765 --> 00:08:20.857
I was the captain.

165
00:08:20.933 --> 00:08:22.764
Yeah.

166
00:08:22.835 --> 00:08:24.735
Um. the aquarium

167
00:08:24.804 --> 00:08:27.671
did a personal appearance deal
with him a couple months ago.

168
00:08:27.740 --> 00:08:30.800
Put him on the ads. built a
Randy LaBayda manta ray tank.

169
00:08:30.877 --> 00:08:34.938
What? And someone wanted him
to be the one to release Shabby.

170
00:08:35.047 --> 00:08:37.208
And you didn't want
that to happen?

171
00:08:37.283 --> 00:08:39.581
Well. no.
It was too soon.

172
00:08:39.652 --> 00:08:42.485
Of course. LaBayda
shanghaied the whole thing.

173
00:08:42.555 --> 00:08:46.685
It was supposed to be a quiet
release with a local photographer.

174
00:08:46.826 --> 00:08:49.522
I got to the dock. the
photographer had been canceled

175
00:08:49.595 --> 00:08:53.622
and I wasn't even allowed on the
boat. No aquarium staff whatsoever.

176
00:08:55.167 --> 00:08:56.691
I never got to
see him again.

177
00:08:56.769 --> 00:08:58.737
So awful.

178
00:09:00.773 --> 00:09:04.402
So. uh. what happened
out on the boat?

179
00:09:04.977 --> 00:09:09.380
Well. no one knows. Everyone
got back late and a little upset.

180
00:09:09.982 --> 00:09:13.281
Then they locked up the ship's log
in LaBayda's office at the aquarium.

181
00:09:13.352 --> 00:09:17.015
April. we're going to need to get into
that office so that I can feel things.

182
00:09:18.591 --> 00:09:19.990
I can get you in.

183
00:09:20.059 --> 00:09:21.458
How soon?

184
00:09:21.827 --> 00:09:23.226
Tonight.

185
00:09:26.999 --> 00:09:28.398
Are you wearing
sweatpants?

186
00:09:28.467 --> 00:09:30.458
These are my
sneaking-around pants.

187
00:09:30.536 --> 00:09:32.367
Don't be jealous.
I got you a matching pair.

188
00:09:32.438 --> 00:09:34.167
You're dressing up for her. Dressing up?

189
00:09:34.240 --> 00:09:37.073
Dude. I'm wearing sweats and
this ridiculous lime-green jacket.

190
00:09:37.143 --> 00:09:38.974
That's my lime-green
jacket. Shawn.

191
00:09:39.045 --> 00:09:40.205
And it's only
for players.

192
00:09:40.279 --> 00:09:42.804
Okay. look. I backed off.
You need to get over it.

193
00:09:42.882 --> 00:09:45.715
Okay. This is it.

194
00:09:47.119 --> 00:09:49.246
What. is there like a
hidden door in the rock wall?

195
00:09:49.655 --> 00:09:51.486
No.

196
00:09:51.557 --> 00:09:52.990
You said you can
get us in.

197
00:09:53.059 --> 00:09:55.254
Yeah. I. uh.
I can give you a boost.

198
00:09:56.028 --> 00:09:58.553
The electrified security
fence is broken here.

199
00:09:58.631 --> 00:10:00.394
Oh. unless they fixed it.

200
00:10:01.934 --> 00:10:03.060
You don't work here?

201
00:10:03.135 --> 00:10:07.697
Well. technically no.
I did. until Tuesday.

202
00:10:07.840 --> 00:10:11.936
I was asking too many questions. and
LaBayda's producer. Tim. had me canned.

203
00:10:12.011 --> 00:10:13.911
Which is why
I asked for your help.

204
00:10:14.413 --> 00:10:16.040
You want us
to scale a wall?

205
00:10:16.115 --> 00:10:17.446
Is it too high?

206
00:10:17.516 --> 00:10:21.350
Oh. no. No. I could probably free
jump it if the ground wasn't so wet.

207
00:10:21.420 --> 00:10:22.546
You could not.
I could vault it.

208
00:10:22.622 --> 00:10:24.453
Where would you land?
Okay. listen.

209
00:10:25.124 --> 00:10:28.025
There's a door right on
the other side of this wall.

210
00:10:28.094 --> 00:10:30.324
It'll lead you straight
towards LaBayda's office.

211
00:10:30.396 --> 00:10:34.992
The code is 1-8-4-2. If I'm
wrong. you can just leave.

212
00:10:35.534 --> 00:10:38.435
If it doesn't work.
we're probably going to jail.

213
00:10:39.472 --> 00:10:40.564
Yeah.

214
00:10:40.873 --> 00:10:42.966
Who's first? Come on.

215
00:10:49.081 --> 00:10:50.844
See? She's legit.

216
00:10:50.916 --> 00:10:53.851
Legit? She just
boosted us over a wall.

217
00:10:53.919 --> 00:10:56.114
She does have very impressive
strength for a girl of her size.

218
00:10:56.188 --> 00:10:59.954
Okay.
Coolest office ever.

219
00:11:03.329 --> 00:11:04.318
Hello!

220
00:11:09.869 --> 00:11:11.393
What's this?

221
00:11:14.840 --> 00:11:17.001
Wait a minute. Dude.

222
00:11:19.311 --> 00:11:23.008
There's two laptops. Why lock
up this laptop over that one?

223
00:11:27.953 --> 00:11:29.944
Why does this
have a GPS on it?

224
00:11:30.022 --> 00:11:33.981
It's the only software on this computer.
And it's not picking up anything.

225
00:11:37.196 --> 00:11:39.994
Can we stop playing with this guy's
computer and get to the ship's log. please?

226
00:11:40.066 --> 00:11:41.795
Knock yourself out.

227
00:11:47.773 --> 00:11:51.072
This is all wrong. They were supposed
to release Shabby near San Miguel Island.

228
00:11:51.143 --> 00:11:52.167
Okay.

229
00:11:52.244 --> 00:11:54.610
Where they let him off is
nowhere near close to that.

230
00:11:54.680 --> 00:11:55.704
Why would they do that?

231
00:11:56.849 --> 00:11:58.248
We need to get
out of here.

232
00:11:59.785 --> 00:12:01.218
Goodbye!

233
00:12:02.088 --> 00:12:03.680
Okay. Let's get out of here. All right.

234
00:12:03.756 --> 00:12:05.087
Oh. wait. there's
one more thing.

235
00:12:05.157 --> 00:12:06.146
What?

236
00:12:06.659 --> 00:12:08.627
I have unfinished
business here.

237
00:12:09.195 --> 00:12:10.662
And a date
with destiny.

238
00:12:13.499 --> 00:12:16.161
No. No! You are not
swimming with the dolphins.

239
00:12:16.235 --> 00:12:17.497
When are we gonna have
another chance. Gus?

240
00:12:17.570 --> 00:12:18.867
I don't care. Shawn.
Come on.

241
00:12:18.938 --> 00:12:20.462
I'm in. I'm on it.
I'm out.

242
00:12:20.539 --> 00:12:23.736
Hopefully they have a harness
or a small saddle of some sort.

243
00:12:23.809 --> 00:12:25.106
I've charged up
my camera.

244
00:12:25.211 --> 00:12:26.838
You don't have to worry about
the flash. It's all digital.

245
00:12:26.912 --> 00:12:29.403
Just keep on snapping.
No. we are leaving. Shawn.

246
00:12:29.482 --> 00:12:32.383
I'm gonna ride that
dolphin into modern history.

247
00:12:32.451 --> 00:12:34.146
I'm going up top.
I'm staying here.

248
00:12:34.620 --> 00:12:36.554
You're missing out on the
opportunity of a lifetime!

249
00:12:36.622 --> 00:12:37.680
Please.

250
00:12:38.124 --> 00:12:40.649
That dolphin is not
gonna ride itself.

251
00:12:40.726 --> 00:12:42.591
Shawn!
Shawn. get back here!

252
00:14:01.073 --> 00:14:02.734
Get out of here.

253
00:14:02.808 --> 00:14:03.968
Not now!

254
00:14:05.277 --> 00:14:06.801
Quiet!

255
00:14:07.947 --> 00:14:09.539
Pa does not love Fa.

256
00:14:11.350 --> 00:14:13.580
No. Pa does not
love Fa.

257
00:14:13.652 --> 00:14:15.244
You're not listening.

258
00:14:15.321 --> 00:14:16.549
I'm sorry.

259
00:14:16.622 --> 00:14:18.055
Stop doing that!

260
00:14:21.293 --> 00:14:22.885
What the hell
are you doing?

261
00:14:22.962 --> 00:14:24.862
Conducting an investigation.
thank you very much.

262
00:14:24.930 --> 00:14:26.022
Then why do you
smell like herring?

263
00:14:26.098 --> 00:14:27.759
Because this is an aquarium.

264
00:14:29.268 --> 00:14:33.034
You're feeding him! We're about to go
to jail and you're training dolphins?

265
00:14:33.105 --> 00:14:37.041
He insisted. I had no choice in the
matter. I said. Pa does not love Fa.

266
00:14:38.210 --> 00:14:41.873
And your hands are filthy. Do you realize
how many germs you can transmit like that?

267
00:14:41.947 --> 00:14:43.039
Here. Give me that.
No.

268
00:14:43.115 --> 00:14:44.377
What? Give...

269
00:14:48.053 --> 00:14:49.213
Here. dolphin.

270
00:14:49.288 --> 00:14:50.880
You just
want to feed him yourself.

271
00:14:50.956 --> 00:14:53.982
I'm getting rid of the evidence.
And. yes. it's not fair that you.

272
00:14:54.059 --> 00:14:55.993
the person who cares less
than me about marine wildlife.

273
00:14:56.061 --> 00:14:57.392
gets to feed them
and I don't.

274
00:14:57.463 --> 00:14:59.021
Just throw it
and let's get out of here.

275
00:14:59.798 --> 00:15:01.789
Don't make a move!

276
00:15:01.901 --> 00:15:05.564
Drop the fish. sir.
and nobody gets hurt.

277
00:15:14.613 --> 00:15:16.740
Breaking and entering?

278
00:15:16.815 --> 00:15:20.273
It was really just entering. Climbing
and entering. We had the code.

279
00:15:20.352 --> 00:15:22.513
Is that a backstage pass?
And a Dolce jacket?

280
00:15:22.588 --> 00:15:24.749
I have third row center
at Phil Collins tonight.

281
00:15:24.857 --> 00:15:26.381
and I get called back here

282
00:15:26.458 --> 00:15:30.451
because my department's psychic wanted to
break into an aquarium to feed some fish?

283
00:15:30.529 --> 00:15:31.928
That is not entirely true.

284
00:15:31.997 --> 00:15:33.726
Then why were you
wearing swim trunks.

285
00:15:33.799 --> 00:15:36.267
<i>carrying a How To Ride
a Dolphin pamphlet?</i>

286
00:15:36.335 --> 00:15:38.826
Chief. that's a long story. The truth
is we're on the trail of something.

287
00:15:38.904 --> 00:15:39.928
Something big.

288
00:15:40.005 --> 00:15:41.905
Something important.
Slightly sexy.

289
00:15:43.042 --> 00:15:45.670
Chief. I think I can
shed some light on this.

290
00:15:45.744 --> 00:15:47.109
This is April McArthur.

291
00:15:47.179 --> 00:15:49.739
I did it.
Yeah. um...

292
00:15:49.815 --> 00:15:51.248
I couldn't let you guys
take the fall for me.

293
00:15:51.317 --> 00:15:55.219
I'm sorry. miss. You broke
into the Santa Barbara Aquarium?

294
00:15:55.287 --> 00:15:59.917
Yeah. well. um. I led them to believe that
I was still an employee at the aquarium.

295
00:15:59.992 --> 00:16:03.689
I got them the code for the alarm
and got them into the facility.

296
00:16:03.762 --> 00:16:07.198
She was also able to inexplicably
lift us over a security wall.

297
00:16:07.266 --> 00:16:09.063
Yeah. Chief. she has a good reason.

298
00:16:09.134 --> 00:16:11.898
She was actually
acting heroically.

299
00:16:11.971 --> 00:16:15.600
Thank you. Juliet. No. thank
you. And I like those earrings.

300
00:16:15.674 --> 00:16:17.869
Chief. there may have
been a murder.

301
00:16:17.943 --> 00:16:19.877
I can't believe
poor Shabby is dead.

302
00:16:19.945 --> 00:16:21.003
You. too. Jules?

303
00:16:21.080 --> 00:16:24.709
Shawn. the ShabbyCam is my screen
saver. We can all learn from him.

304
00:16:24.783 --> 00:16:26.978
Wait. wait. wait.
Who's Shabby?

305
00:16:27.052 --> 00:16:28.542
You don't want to know.
I don't?

306
00:16:28.620 --> 00:16:32.078
Yeah. probably not. Just know
I am taking lead on this case.

307
00:16:32.157 --> 00:16:35.649
There is a crime at play. Trust me. I
will straighten out these aquarium people.

308
00:16:35.728 --> 00:16:39.186
They do not want to press charges
at all. They like her. And so do I.

309
00:16:39.264 --> 00:16:41.755
We do not want to arrest this
woman. We need to help her.

310
00:16:41.834 --> 00:16:45.361
Wow! Well. thank you
for that endorsement. O'Hara.

311
00:16:45.437 --> 00:16:49.430
Now. I have to get back to the
Bowl. Somebody needs to take me.

312
00:16:49.508 --> 00:16:53.274
<i>because if I miss Against All Odds.
then somebody is getting fired.</i>

313
00:16:54.813 --> 00:16:57.611
I missed it?
They released you already?

314
00:16:58.083 --> 00:17:01.143
Lassy. it was all a big
misunderstanding. We're working a case.

315
00:17:01.220 --> 00:17:02.653
Jules is helping out.

316
00:17:02.721 --> 00:17:04.848
We are solving
a heinous crime.

317
00:17:04.923 --> 00:17:07.824
Heinous crime?
Wait a minute.

318
00:17:09.028 --> 00:17:10.222
How heinous?

319
00:17:10.829 --> 00:17:14.230
Look. it's not a big deal. There may
have been a murder. We've got it covered.

320
00:17:14.299 --> 00:17:15.391
I just need a name.

321
00:17:16.201 --> 00:17:17.225
I'd rather not.

322
00:17:17.503 --> 00:17:20.768
Listen. You guys don't know what I've
been through these last couple weeks.

323
00:17:20.839 --> 00:17:22.397
I chased down a group
of diamond smugglers.

324
00:17:22.474 --> 00:17:23.941
Congratulations.
Not exactly.

325
00:17:24.009 --> 00:17:26.842
I chased them to an airport. where
a plane was waiting for them. Wait.

326
00:17:27.646 --> 00:17:29.614
What does "Rocinante"
mean to you?

327
00:17:29.681 --> 00:17:31.774
A full-bodied Syrah. A
gay couple from Lisbon?

328
00:17:31.850 --> 00:17:34.284
No. it was the name of their plane.
It flew off into a lightning storm.

329
00:17:34.353 --> 00:17:36.947
I wanted to chase them. but
apparently our helicopters only fly

330
00:17:37.022 --> 00:17:39.149
<i>when there's rainbows in the
sky. so they got away clean.</i>

331
00:17:39.224 --> 00:17:41.454
which mean I'm officially
jackass number one around here.

332
00:17:41.527 --> 00:17:42.789
I need a case.

333
00:17:44.096 --> 00:17:46.223
Give me
the victim's name.

334
00:17:51.103 --> 00:17:52.434
Shabby.
Shabby.

335
00:17:53.005 --> 00:17:54.472
Is that a street name?

336
00:17:54.540 --> 00:17:56.235
It's more of a given name.

337
00:17:56.742 --> 00:17:58.539
Last name?
He doesn't have one.

338
00:17:58.610 --> 00:18:00.475
Do not play with me.

339
00:18:01.013 --> 00:18:02.776
Can I spell it?
I don't care.

340
00:18:04.416 --> 00:18:06.350
T- H-E.
T- H-E...

341
00:18:06.919 --> 00:18:08.784
S- E-A.
... S -E-A...

342
00:18:08.854 --> 00:18:10.344
L- I-O...

343
00:18:12.691 --> 00:18:13.680
N?

344
00:18:14.226 --> 00:18:15.716
<i>Thesealion?</i>

345
00:18:16.061 --> 00:18:17.858
What is that? French?

346
00:18:18.831 --> 00:18:19.855
Pinniped.

347
00:18:19.932 --> 00:18:23.060
Pinniped? Never heard of
it. All right. description?

348
00:18:23.135 --> 00:18:24.159
Black.

349
00:18:24.236 --> 00:18:25.362
Black. Height and weight?

350
00:18:25.437 --> 00:18:27.598
Six. seven hundred pounds.

351
00:18:27.673 --> 00:18:28.731
Jeez. Louise!

352
00:18:28.807 --> 00:18:30.468
Listen.
can you get a body exhumed?

353
00:18:30.542 --> 00:18:33.443
Of course I can. As long
as I'm in on the autopsy.

354
00:18:40.085 --> 00:18:41.780
I'm going to
kill you. Spencer.

355
00:18:41.854 --> 00:18:44.823
I never told you that the
victim wasn't a sea lion.

356
00:18:44.957 --> 00:18:46.891
Carlton. I tried to
keep you out of this.

357
00:18:46.959 --> 00:18:48.290
Uh. how long
is this gonna take?

358
00:18:48.360 --> 00:18:51.659
I don't know. I've never examined
one of these things before.

359
00:18:51.730 --> 00:18:53.095
Okay. that's fair.

360
00:18:53.398 --> 00:18:56.561
Are there any signs of. uh...
I don't know. foul play?

361
00:18:56.635 --> 00:18:58.728
Well. a couple of things
are odd.

362
00:18:58.804 --> 00:19:00.863
I found a strange
empty piercing.

363
00:19:00.939 --> 00:19:02.964
Maybe he started swimming
with the wrong crowd.

364
00:19:03.041 --> 00:19:04.906
You didn't happen to
find any tattoos. did you?

365
00:19:04.977 --> 00:19:05.966
Carlton!

366
00:19:06.044 --> 00:19:08.774
Well. I found some flat
reef coral in the fur.

367
00:19:08.881 --> 00:19:09.939
How is that possible?

368
00:19:10.015 --> 00:19:11.846
Yeah! Coral!
In the ocean!

369
00:19:11.917 --> 00:19:13.441
Are you really
asking that question?

370
00:19:13.519 --> 00:19:15.316
A sea lion
is a precision animal.

371
00:19:15.387 --> 00:19:17.719
It knows how to swim around a
reef without thrashing into it.

372
00:19:17.789 --> 00:19:18.881
That's true.

373
00:19:18.957 --> 00:19:21.357
And I found some
synthetic fibers.

374
00:19:21.727 --> 00:19:23.820
Okay! What kind
of fibers?

375
00:19:23.896 --> 00:19:26.558
Monofilament line. The
kind found in fishing nets?

376
00:19:26.632 --> 00:19:29.294
All right. I've heard enough. Close
this thing up. Let's go. O'Hara.

377
00:19:29.368 --> 00:19:31.336
Lassy. you're not being
very helpful right now.

378
00:19:31.403 --> 00:19:33.633
Really? Well. let me see if I can
close this case for you right now.

379
00:19:33.705 --> 00:19:37.197
Now. I'm no expert. but let me
take a shot. You've got a sea lion.

380
00:19:37.276 --> 00:19:40.837
and you've got a net and you've got
the ocean. You put them all together.

381
00:19:41.079 --> 00:19:42.307
case closed.

382
00:19:48.520 --> 00:19:49.748
What?

383
00:19:49.821 --> 00:19:51.448
I'm worried
he might be right.

384
00:19:51.523 --> 00:19:53.548
Are you serious?
I don't know. Gus.

385
00:19:54.793 --> 00:19:57.819
We definitely need to see that reef.
And I know how we can get out there.

386
00:20:05.370 --> 00:20:07.964
All right. That's it. that's it.
Your hands are at ten and two.

387
00:20:08.040 --> 00:20:09.667
Down there. that's
your trim tab.

388
00:20:09.741 --> 00:20:12.539
Over there. your heat gauge.
That's your fish finder. GPS.

389
00:20:12.611 --> 00:20:14.772
Uses waypoints. just like in a
car when you find a place you like.

390
00:20:14.846 --> 00:20:17.212
Look at that. You got a little
microwave down there. Would you... Shawn!

391
00:20:17.282 --> 00:20:19.307
Please focus.
Look forward.

392
00:20:19.384 --> 00:20:21.352
Do not become complacent
just because it's water.

393
00:20:22.354 --> 00:20:23.981
Dad. we're still
in the dock.

394
00:20:24.957 --> 00:20:27.050
Look. Shawn. Do you wanna
drive this thing or not?

395
00:20:27.125 --> 00:20:29.252
I never asked that!
Isn't that right. Gus?

396
00:20:29.328 --> 00:20:31.023
Yeah. I'm gonna get
in the middle of that.

397
00:20:31.096 --> 00:20:34.793
Man. I just wanted to come see your
new boat. go out onto the reef...

398
00:20:34.866 --> 00:20:35.890
The reef?

399
00:20:35.968 --> 00:20:37.868
I'm not going out on the reef.
That place is restricted waters.

400
00:20:37.936 --> 00:20:39.301
What if I told you
it was for a case?

401
00:20:39.371 --> 00:20:40.497
Well. that would
make it worse.

402
00:20:40.739 --> 00:20:41.763
What if he didn't?

403
00:20:41.840 --> 00:20:43.865
Look. we won't tell anyone.
okay? We totally promise.

404
00:20:43.942 --> 00:20:45.569
Plus. it'll totally
solve a crime.

405
00:20:45.644 --> 00:20:48.738
Shawn. would you please listen to
me? I'm not going out onto the reef.

406
00:20:48.814 --> 00:20:51.476
That place is off-limits to people.
I'm not going to lose my boat.

407
00:20:51.550 --> 00:20:55.008
I'm not gonna lose my license to follow
some stupid. lame-ass hunch of yours.

408
00:20:55.087 --> 00:20:56.213
You're really not
gonna budge on this?

409
00:20:56.288 --> 00:20:57.687
What do you think?

410
00:20:58.857 --> 00:20:59.881
Told you.

411
00:20:59.958 --> 00:21:02.950
All right! All right! I do!
I wanna learn how to drive.

412
00:21:03.028 --> 00:21:06.191
Shawn. hold up a second.
I wanna grab my tackle box.

413
00:21:09.901 --> 00:21:12.267
Shawn! Shawn! No!
Shawn!

414
00:21:12.337 --> 00:21:13.702
Don't worry. it's cool. It's
cool. What are you doing?

415
00:21:13.772 --> 00:21:15.171
Get back here!

416
00:21:15.574 --> 00:21:16.563
He's gonna come
after us!

417
00:21:16.642 --> 00:21:19.372
No. he can't swim that fast.
Besides. he wanted me to do this.

418
00:21:19.444 --> 00:21:20.672
Shawn!

419
00:21:20.746 --> 00:21:23.237
He wanted you to steal his boat? Yeah.

420
00:21:23.448 --> 00:21:25.916
He didn't want to be responsible for
crossing over into restricted waters.

421
00:21:25.984 --> 00:21:27.008
Shawn! Get back here!

422
00:21:27.085 --> 00:21:29.952
Didn't you get that with the whole. "Shawn.
Shawn. let me show you how to drive"?

423
00:21:30.022 --> 00:21:31.922
I think he wanted to
show you how to drive.

424
00:21:31.990 --> 00:21:33.321
Yeah. so I could
steal it later.

425
00:21:44.169 --> 00:21:47.969
This thing's all numbers. It's very
hard to read. Maybe it's upside down.

426
00:21:48.040 --> 00:21:50.167
<i>First of all. Shawn.
that's a Thomas Guide.</i>

427
00:21:50.242 --> 00:21:53.234
Ah! I thought it was a
little land-heavy. But look.

428
00:21:53.312 --> 00:21:55.940
I think the reef is down
here in the corner. A-7.

429
00:21:56.014 --> 00:21:59.245
Did you listen to anything your
dad said? The map is the screen.

430
00:21:59.318 --> 00:22:02.651
Gus. don't be exactly half of
an 11-pound black forest ham.

431
00:22:03.221 --> 00:22:04.620
That's clearly the GPS.

432
00:22:04.690 --> 00:22:08.182
Exactly. It's latitude and
longitude. You follow the degrees.

433
00:22:08.493 --> 00:22:09.687
Oh. yeah?

434
00:22:10.195 --> 00:22:12.288
Those numbers with the little
quotation marks there?

435
00:22:12.364 --> 00:22:13.353
Yes.

436
00:22:17.536 --> 00:22:19.527
Dude! I think I know
where it may have gone down.

437
00:22:19.604 --> 00:22:23.472
That laptop was probably tracking
LaBayda's boat. Here. Here. Punch this in.

438
00:22:24.443 --> 00:22:26.138
34 degrees.
zero-six.

439
00:22:26.211 --> 00:22:27.872
<i>and then. uh. one of those
little lines that I would use</i>

440
00:22:27.946 --> 00:22:30.471
<i>to. uh. to make a
winky face in a text.</i>

441
00:22:30.549 --> 00:22:31.573
No. no. no.
go back. go back.

442
00:22:31.650 --> 00:22:33.208
It should be the left eye
that's winking. not the right.

443
00:22:33.285 --> 00:22:34.309
No... Gus.

444
00:22:34.386 --> 00:22:35.819
pretend the person doesn't
even have a right eye.

445
00:22:35.887 --> 00:22:38.481
No ocular socket
whatsoever. Sutured shut.

446
00:22:38.557 --> 00:22:39.785
From birth.
Shawn. I got it.

447
00:22:39.858 --> 00:22:42.520
Yes! That's it. right there. That's
good. Okay. Now. 50 degrees...

448
00:22:43.462 --> 00:22:44.656
Come on. buddy!

449
00:22:47.165 --> 00:22:51.067
Two degrees to the right.
No. Up. Two degrees up.

450
00:22:51.136 --> 00:22:52.626
What do those two
little dots mean again?

451
00:22:52.704 --> 00:22:55.639
Kick out the lights. Oh. dude. we're
getting close. Right on top of it.

452
00:22:55.707 --> 00:22:57.675
Kick out the lights. Why am
I gonna kick out the lights?

453
00:22:57.743 --> 00:22:59.904
I think I see another boat
out in the distance.

454
00:23:00.445 --> 00:23:02.379
Where is another boat? It
doesn't matter where. Shawn.

455
00:23:02.447 --> 00:23:03.778
We're in
restricted waters.

456
00:23:03.849 --> 00:23:05.578
I can't get arrested twice
in the same week.

457
00:23:05.784 --> 00:23:07.979
You might have a few arrests
in you. but I don't. Okay. Fine.

458
00:23:16.695 --> 00:23:18.287
Did you hear
something?

459
00:23:18.363 --> 00:23:19.557
Like what?

460
00:23:19.865 --> 00:23:22.333
Like voices.

461
00:23:27.806 --> 00:23:29.000
Take him!
What?

462
00:23:29.074 --> 00:23:30.473
I had this dream
before. Shawn.

463
00:23:30.542 --> 00:23:32.806
<i>Ever since we saw Dead Calm. You
have to take one for the team.</i>

464
00:23:32.878 --> 00:23:34.277
What are you talking about?
Take one for the team!

465
00:23:34.346 --> 00:23:36.405
But no one's gonna hurt us. Hey. guys.

466
00:23:36.481 --> 00:23:38.881
These are restricted waters.
What the heck you doing out here?

467
00:23:38.950 --> 00:23:43.751
Ahoy there! Um. yes. Right.
Uh. my name is Shawn Spencer.

468
00:23:43.989 --> 00:23:46.924
This is my first mate.
Hummingbird Saltalamaccia. Hello!

469
00:23:47.793 --> 00:23:50.489
We were turned around.
Discombobulated.

470
00:23:50.562 --> 00:23:52.689
We just now realized that
we're in restricted waters.

471
00:23:52.764 --> 00:23:55.460
Just now. And we both
have hepatitis.

472
00:23:55.534 --> 00:23:58.970
I also couldn't help but notice
you are not the Coast Guard.

473
00:23:59.104 --> 00:24:02.267
No. No. we thought you were the
Coast Guard coming to tow us in.

474
00:24:02.340 --> 00:24:03.671
Us?
Yeah.

475
00:24:03.742 --> 00:24:05.573
No. no.

476
00:24:05.644 --> 00:24:08.613
But does that mean that they're
coming? And if so. do you have an ETA?

477
00:24:08.680 --> 00:24:11.615
No. No idea. We just... we've been.
uh. drifting for about an hour.

478
00:24:11.683 --> 00:24:13.310
We stalled on our way
to Monterey.

479
00:24:13.385 --> 00:24:15.785
<i>Ah! Old Mexico.</i>

480
00:24:15.854 --> 00:24:18.482
Monterrey. Mexico is 2.000
miles inland. Shawn.

481
00:24:18.557 --> 00:24:22.653
Up north. So. what are
you guys doing out here?

482
00:24:22.727 --> 00:24:26.390
Oh. you know. Just. uh.
hiding from sharks.

483
00:24:26.465 --> 00:24:28.558
Yeah. we heard that they can
see you if your lights are on.

484
00:24:28.667 --> 00:24:30.134
so we kicked ours off.

485
00:24:30.202 --> 00:24:33.433
Uh. that's not how
sharks work at all.

486
00:24:33.505 --> 00:24:37.669
Regular sharks. Of course. Right.
But we heard there was an infestation

487
00:24:37.742 --> 00:24:42.839
of genetically-altered. shark-like
beasts here. in this area of the water.

488
00:24:43.148 --> 00:24:44.672
They can smell the light.

489
00:24:44.749 --> 00:24:46.341
They also type. True.

490
00:24:46.418 --> 00:24:48.147
What?
Not well.

491
00:24:48.587 --> 00:24:52.614
But they're sharks. with fins.
so it's still impressive.

492
00:24:53.592 --> 00:24:57.187
Oh. and. uh. how long did you say
before the Coast Guard gets here?

493
00:24:57.262 --> 00:25:00.527
They're not just right around
the corner or anything. are they?

494
00:25:02.133 --> 00:25:04.624
I'm telling you. Gus. there's
something wrong with those guys.

495
00:25:04.703 --> 00:25:06.466
Did you want to stay out
there and chat it up with them?

496
00:25:06.538 --> 00:25:10.372
No. but we may not be the only ones out
there looking for the sea lion's killer.

497
00:25:11.076 --> 00:25:12.338
Uh-uh.

498
00:25:13.445 --> 00:25:15.106
Maybe he didn't want me
to take the boat.

499
00:25:15.180 --> 00:25:16.306
I'm jumping out here.

500
00:25:16.381 --> 00:25:17.575
Okay. but you're
gonna get wet.

501
00:25:18.583 --> 00:25:21.313
I can't believe this. Shawn. I'm gonna
get arrested two times in one week.

502
00:25:22.487 --> 00:25:25.684
Okay. Dad. we have to come up
with a system for unspoken actions.

503
00:25:25.757 --> 00:25:27.315
I can't believe
you called the cops.

504
00:25:27.392 --> 00:25:30.088
I didn't call them. Shawn.
They called me.

505
00:25:30.161 --> 00:25:31.219
Why?

506
00:25:31.296 --> 00:25:32.695
The coroner finished
his inquiry.

507
00:25:32.764 --> 00:25:34.629
Found a bullet
inside the sea lion.

508
00:25:35.600 --> 00:25:37.761
Two. 22 slugs. actually.

509
00:25:37.836 --> 00:25:38.894
He was shot?

510
00:25:38.970 --> 00:25:40.028
He was murdered.

511
00:25:49.080 --> 00:25:52.709
So. am I gonna need a lawyer?
'Cause mine's on a boat.

512
00:25:52.918 --> 00:25:55.682
Off Cape Horn.
It might take a while.

513
00:25:56.521 --> 00:25:59.786
Mister LaBayda. would you remove
that bird from your shoulder?

514
00:25:59.858 --> 00:26:02.827
Oh. this is an
Australian hissing owl.

515
00:26:02.894 --> 00:26:06.330
And I have to do a show with
him in about three hours.

516
00:26:06.398 --> 00:26:10.232
If I haven't bonded with him by then.
he will spend the entire shoot crapping

517
00:26:10.302 --> 00:26:12.293
all over my Ed Hardy tee.

518
00:26:12.370 --> 00:26:16.238
Now. I would appreciate it
if you'd watch your tone.

519
00:26:16.308 --> 00:26:17.969
'Cause this thing
is like a sponge

520
00:26:18.043 --> 00:26:22.412
and he can get really
aggressive when things get tense.

521
00:26:23.548 --> 00:26:24.708
Detective. telephone.

522
00:26:24.783 --> 00:26:27.581
I'm in the middle of
something. It's the FBI.

523
00:26:27.652 --> 00:26:28.676
Again? Would you
tell them

524
00:26:28.753 --> 00:26:31.051
I didn't know they were
smugglers until it was too late?

525
00:26:31.122 --> 00:26:34.023
<i>And tell them if I had access to my own
plane. I could have followed the Rocinante</i>

526
00:26:34.092 --> 00:26:36.253
into the storm! Maybe you
should tell them yourself.

527
00:26:37.429 --> 00:26:38.418
Right.

528
00:26:44.402 --> 00:26:46.927
Didn't I have her fired?

529
00:26:47.906 --> 00:26:50.466
Oh! Is that your source?

530
00:26:50.542 --> 00:26:54.171
No. Mr. LaBayda.
our source is the court.

531
00:26:54.245 --> 00:26:57.043
as in a court-sanctioned
search we did of your office.

532
00:26:57.115 --> 00:26:59.345
We found animal-tracking
software on your computer.

533
00:26:59.417 --> 00:27:01.214
We don't tag
our animals. Randy!

534
00:27:01.286 --> 00:27:03.652
Once they're released
into the wild. they're free.

535
00:27:04.289 --> 00:27:06.382
Perhaps you'd like
to explain.

536
00:27:10.261 --> 00:27:11.455
I need someone
to take the bird.

537
00:27:14.265 --> 00:27:15.425
All right.

538
00:27:16.701 --> 00:27:18.032
We were going to track him.

539
00:27:18.136 --> 00:27:21.867
But it was such a great.
heartwarming local story.

540
00:27:21.940 --> 00:27:23.271
It would have been
a great national one.

541
00:27:23.341 --> 00:27:24.808
I mean you can't
blame me for

542
00:27:25.677 --> 00:27:28.043
wanting the people to
know what happened to this

543
00:27:28.713 --> 00:27:30.704
special creature.

544
00:27:30.782 --> 00:27:35.185
Yeah. Well. we need to know
why you released him miles away

545
00:27:35.253 --> 00:27:37.050
from where you were
supposed to.

546
00:27:40.692 --> 00:27:41.954
I. uh.

547
00:27:43.294 --> 00:27:45.421
think I'd like to
make my phone call now.

548
00:27:45.497 --> 00:27:47.727
Yeah. I bet you would.

549
00:27:51.102 --> 00:27:52.228
LaBayda's Sea Adventure.

550
00:27:53.638 --> 00:27:54.969
Burn the disks.

551
00:27:55.106 --> 00:27:56.095
Is this you. boss?

552
00:27:56.908 --> 00:27:58.375
Destroy the footage.

553
00:27:58.443 --> 00:28:01.810
Take a vacation in Mexico for
at least a week. Can you do that?

554
00:28:01.880 --> 00:28:04.371
<i>I can't get to the footage
right now. Chief. Why not?</i>

555
00:28:05.183 --> 00:28:06.912
Because your two hair analysts
are reviewing it right now.

556
00:28:07.519 --> 00:28:10.386
I don't have
a hair analyst!

557
00:28:10.789 --> 00:28:12.120
<i>Who set that up?</i>

558
00:28:12.390 --> 00:28:13.652
Oh. crap.

559
00:28:14.526 --> 00:28:16.255
<i>Get over there! Now!</i>

560
00:28:18.296 --> 00:28:20.264
Hair analyst?
That worked?

561
00:28:20.331 --> 00:28:21.992
I've always dreamed
of having one myself.

562
00:28:22.067 --> 00:28:26.834
<i>I need the sunset perfectly
framing the silhouette.</i>

563
00:28:27.372 --> 00:28:29.772
<i>It has to be me
and the wild.</i>

564
00:28:30.475 --> 00:28:34.468
<i>Now. let me just say. you see a
single strand of my hair out of place.</i>

565
00:28:35.080 --> 00:28:37.571
<i>let me know. We cut right then and
there. And that includes chest hair.</i>

566
00:28:37.949 --> 00:28:39.177
<i>Tim. you got me?
You got me?</i>

567
00:28:39.250 --> 00:28:40.945
<i>Yeah. I got it.
All right. Here we go.</i>

568
00:28:41.019 --> 00:28:42.680
<i>All right. Three... What?</i>

569
00:28:42.754 --> 00:28:44.346
<i>Freighter. freighter.
What?</i>

570
00:28:44.556 --> 00:28:48.492
<i>No! No! Get out
of the way!</i>

571
00:28:48.560 --> 00:28:51.427
<i>Get your big polluting ass
out of my shot!</i>

572
00:28:51.496 --> 00:28:53.589
<i>How many boats
are there gonna be?</i>

573
00:28:55.700 --> 00:28:57.861
<i>Okay! Perfect.</i>

574
00:28:59.003 --> 00:29:00.766
<i>I guess this'll
just have to do.</i>

575
00:29:03.108 --> 00:29:07.101
<i>I don't like it. I wanna go on
record saying. "I don't like it. "</i>

576
00:29:07.746 --> 00:29:11.773
Gus. he's not a murderer.
He's just an egomaniac.

577
00:29:11.916 --> 00:29:13.543
And for fairly good reason.
His hair is spectacular.

578
00:29:14.953 --> 00:29:17.820
<i>Swim. Swim. my friend.</i>

579
00:29:17.956 --> 00:29:21.016
He released Shabby in the wrong
place to get a better shot!

580
00:29:22.026 --> 00:29:24.460
That means Shabby was just in
the wrong place at the wrong time.

581
00:29:25.063 --> 00:29:29.557
<i>Arrivederci. my furry
little Michael Phelps.</i>

582
00:29:30.135 --> 00:29:31.466
Arrivederci.

583
00:29:31.536 --> 00:29:34.061
He didn't shoot him.
He didn't do it.

584
00:29:35.073 --> 00:29:39.601
<i>Yeah. pumas are pretty mean. I
know one time I ran into a puma.</i>

585
00:29:40.945 --> 00:29:42.207
<i>Oh. man. I was...</i>

586
00:29:42.280 --> 00:29:46.114
Gus. look at that. That's the
same boat we saw. The same guys!

587
00:29:47.285 --> 00:29:48.843
It was five days ago.

588
00:29:49.420 --> 00:29:51.820
We've been drifting
for about an hour.

589
00:29:51.956 --> 00:29:53.355
We stalled on our way
to Monterey.

590
00:29:54.726 --> 00:29:56.387
They weren't on the way
to Monterey.

591
00:29:56.461 --> 00:29:57.723
They were on their way
to the reef.

592
00:29:57.796 --> 00:29:59.957
The reef where Shabby
went off the grid.

593
00:30:00.031 --> 00:30:01.396
Why would they be going
out there at night?

594
00:30:02.767 --> 00:30:04.860
Guys? Out of there!

595
00:30:05.703 --> 00:30:07.261
Plan "A" or plan "B"?
"B."

596
00:30:07.338 --> 00:30:08.771
Get out of there!

597
00:30:12.610 --> 00:30:14.544
Oh. my God.
I killed him!

598
00:30:23.388 --> 00:30:25.618
Shawn. you can't steal your
dad's boat for a second time.

599
00:30:25.690 --> 00:30:28.818
Gus. you don't understand.
My dad wants me to do this.

600
00:30:30.662 --> 00:30:32.186
Do I. Shawn?

601
00:30:37.368 --> 00:30:39.632
You were really
good with him.

602
00:30:39.704 --> 00:30:43.105
So were you. You really
scared him. And the bird.

603
00:30:45.677 --> 00:30:51.115
Listen. I don't know if this is the
right time to ask. but what about Shawn?

604
00:30:51.649 --> 00:30:53.446
What about him?

605
00:30:53.518 --> 00:30:55.850
I don't know.
Something

606
00:30:56.654 --> 00:30:57.985
intriguing.

607
00:30:58.590 --> 00:31:00.683
You know. odd.
It's refreshing.

608
00:31:01.492 --> 00:31:04.689
I was thinking of letting him
know that I'm. uh. "available. "

609
00:31:04.929 --> 00:31:07.420
You know. and all
that. What do you think?

610
00:31:07.799 --> 00:31:10.996
I don't know.

611
00:31:11.069 --> 00:31:12.161
Is there a problem?

612
00:31:12.237 --> 00:31:14.205
No. No. there's no problem.

613
00:31:16.441 --> 00:31:17.601
Your dad's getting
pretty good.

614
00:31:17.675 --> 00:31:21.577
Too good. I think he's been waiting in
there since Thursday. It's pretty creepy.

615
00:31:21.646 --> 00:31:23.079
And mildly impressive.

616
00:31:24.916 --> 00:31:27.544
Gus. Opportunity.

617
00:31:39.664 --> 00:31:41.529
They're going that way. We
gonna follow them or not?

618
00:31:41.599 --> 00:31:43.658
Uh. I'm definitely a
"not" right now. But...

619
00:31:45.937 --> 00:31:47.131
They might be
coming back.

620
00:31:47.272 --> 00:31:49.638
Walking in the opposite direction.
I think this is our best opportunity.

621
00:31:49.707 --> 00:31:50.696
But they're going
to get help.

622
00:31:50.775 --> 00:31:52.106
They're unloading stuff.

623
00:31:52.210 --> 00:31:53.199
Barnacle Bill.
What...

624
00:31:53.278 --> 00:31:54.267
Shawn!

625
00:31:56.948 --> 00:31:58.381
You wanna be Hawkeye
or Crow's Nest?

626
00:31:58.449 --> 00:31:59.848
What do either
of those mean?

627
00:31:59.918 --> 00:32:01.146
I don't know.
I was hoping you did.

628
00:32:05.857 --> 00:32:07.290
What is all this stuff?

629
00:32:07.358 --> 00:32:11.954
GPS. radar. sonar. electronic
pulse sensors. High-tech stuff.

630
00:32:12.864 --> 00:32:14.695
That's how they knew
we were in the water.

631
00:32:14.766 --> 00:32:16.996
Whatever they were doing.
they didn't want to be found.

632
00:32:19.637 --> 00:32:21.468
And they were
doing it at night.

633
00:32:21.539 --> 00:32:22.801
It's just a bunch
of salvage equipment.

634
00:32:23.608 --> 00:32:24.905
Wait a minute.

635
00:32:35.753 --> 00:32:36.777
We need to get this thing off.

636
00:32:44.162 --> 00:32:45.186
What are we looking for?

637
00:32:45.263 --> 00:32:46.992
This thing! This thing!
This thing!

638
00:32:47.065 --> 00:32:49.124
Here. Let me do it.
I was a Navy scout.

639
00:32:51.536 --> 00:32:52.935
This is a satellite
tracking tag.

640
00:32:53.004 --> 00:32:54.028
What's it for?

641
00:32:54.105 --> 00:32:56.733
They use it for tagging
animals. Training. research.

642
00:32:56.808 --> 00:32:58.673
Well. a couple
of things are odd.

643
00:32:59.210 --> 00:33:00.871
I found a strange
empty piercing.

644
00:33:01.713 --> 00:33:03.010
<i>Why does this
have a GPS on it?</i>

645
00:33:03.915 --> 00:33:05.906
LaBayda was tracking
the sea lion.

646
00:33:09.120 --> 00:33:11.088
He found a bullet
inside the sea lion.

647
00:33:12.090 --> 00:33:13.785
Two. 22 slugs. actually.

648
00:33:17.128 --> 00:33:19.153
They killed him. Shawn.
But why?

649
00:33:19.897 --> 00:33:21.023
We should go.

650
00:33:23.001 --> 00:33:24.866
They're coming. They're gonna
see us! Quick! Jump in the water.

651
00:33:24.936 --> 00:33:26.267
Okay. Hang from the
anchor. Where's the anchor?

652
00:33:26.337 --> 00:33:27.531
That only works
in cartoons.

653
00:33:27.605 --> 00:33:28.594
Is there a shark cage?

654
00:33:28.673 --> 00:33:30.004
How could that
possibly be a good idea?

655
00:33:30.074 --> 00:33:31.769
I don't know! At least I'm
coming up with some ideas!

656
00:33:34.212 --> 00:33:36.976
I'm telling you. I saw the boat
rocking. I swear. It's fine!

657
00:33:40.685 --> 00:33:41.947
There's no one.
Everything's fine.

658
00:33:42.020 --> 00:33:43.214
I saw something.
I'm telling you.

659
00:33:44.088 --> 00:33:47.387
You're paranoid. man. We're in the
home stretch here. Let's go. Get going.

660
00:33:47.458 --> 00:33:50.018
No. I'm not.
I'm checking the pull.

661
00:33:50.094 --> 00:33:53.860
<i>Dude. this is like Out
of Sight. but super gay.</i>

662
00:33:53.931 --> 00:33:55.125
Don't touch me. Shawn.

663
00:33:55.199 --> 00:33:58.066
Wait! Wait! You hear that?

664
00:33:58.136 --> 00:33:59.364
Hear what?

665
00:34:01.239 --> 00:34:03.571
All right. All right.
I'm just nervous. man.

666
00:34:03.975 --> 00:34:05.101
I see a flashlight.

667
00:34:15.186 --> 00:34:17.086
Don't touch me. Shawn.

668
00:34:23.861 --> 00:34:26.796
Wait. What does "Rocinante"
mean to you?

669
00:34:27.098 --> 00:34:29.726
<i>No. It's the name of their airplane.
It flew off into a lightning storm.</i>

670
00:34:30.802 --> 00:34:32.929
Dude! I solved it!
Will you be quiet?

671
00:34:33.004 --> 00:34:34.596
But I solved it!
Be quiet!

672
00:34:34.672 --> 00:34:37.800
Hey! I heard it again.
Didn't you hear that?

673
00:34:37.875 --> 00:34:39.502
What do you hear?

674
00:34:39.577 --> 00:34:41.044
I hear birds!
Listen! Listen!

675
00:34:41.112 --> 00:34:43.979
Untie. push off.
Please. We're going.

676
00:34:47.418 --> 00:34:48.942
I think
that's the engine.

677
00:34:49.020 --> 00:34:50.817
I'm gonna kill you. Shawn.

678
00:34:55.026 --> 00:34:56.653
Okay. I think they're gone.
I'm gonna call for help.

679
00:34:56.727 --> 00:34:58.695
No. He'll hear you.
He has eagle ears.

680
00:34:58.763 --> 00:35:00.355
Eagle ears?
Yes.

681
00:35:00.431 --> 00:35:01.762
How about I send a text?

682
00:35:01.833 --> 00:35:03.801
Mute your keys!
How do I do that?

683
00:35:04.669 --> 00:35:07.433
Come here! Okay. what?
What? What's so important?

684
00:35:07.505 --> 00:35:08.767
I just got a text
from Shawn Spencer.

685
00:35:08.840 --> 00:35:11.775
And what did it say? It says
that he solved the crime. and...

686
00:35:11.843 --> 00:35:13.310
And what?

687
00:35:13.411 --> 00:35:16.778
He's trapped in the hull of a
smuggler's boat going out to sea.

688
00:35:17.782 --> 00:35:19.579
What do we do
with that?

689
00:35:19.650 --> 00:35:21.550
"How can we find... "

690
00:35:21.619 --> 00:35:25.077
Okay. now type the letter "U" instead
Y-O-U. and you don't need that punctuation.

691
00:35:25.156 --> 00:35:26.214
It's just faster.
Chief.

692
00:35:27.792 --> 00:35:30.124
Dude. I really do feel
so Clooney right now.

693
00:35:30.795 --> 00:35:32.695
I am not Jennifer Lopez.

694
00:35:32.763 --> 00:35:33.787
That was a compliment.

695
00:35:33.865 --> 00:35:35.696
How is that
possibly a compliment?

696
00:35:36.234 --> 00:35:39.067
<i>Did you see El Cantante?
She was amazing.</i>

697
00:35:39.670 --> 00:35:40.728
Shawn.

698
00:35:42.840 --> 00:35:45.434
Shabby's
transmitter.

699
00:35:45.510 --> 00:35:47.569
Don't...
Hold on.

700
00:35:47.645 --> 00:35:49.203
Get off me. Shawn.
Get off me.

701
00:35:49.280 --> 00:35:50.269
Got it!

702
00:35:54.318 --> 00:35:56.252
Ooh! Ooh!
I got another text!

703
00:35:56.320 --> 00:35:59.016
What does it say?
"Turn on LaBayda's laptop. "

704
00:35:59.090 --> 00:36:01.115
Uh... Someone get it
out of evidence!

705
00:36:01.959 --> 00:36:05.019
Now
all we do is wait.

706
00:36:06.697 --> 00:36:08.324
Gus. scratch my leg.

707
00:36:09.367 --> 00:36:11.392
Just... Would you just scratch
my leg? I'm not scratching.

708
00:36:11.469 --> 00:36:14.666
The elastic on my sock... I'm
not scratching your leg. Shawn.

709
00:36:15.306 --> 00:36:17.171
Can you give us a general
location of the boat?

710
00:36:17.241 --> 00:36:19.038
Well. it's a little bit problematic.

711
00:36:19.110 --> 00:36:22.204
